{"id":"project-LICHEN-worker6-x6op.3","title":"AES key construction lacks length assertion","description":"File: oscore/src/edhoc/initiator.rs:441

Issue: `AesCcm::new_from_slice(&k_3)` returns an error if `k_3.len() != KEY_LEN` (16 bytes), but the error is mapped to `InvalidState` which is misleading. More critically, there is no upfront assertion that `k_3` has the correct length.

Trigger: If `edhoc_kdf` returns fewer bytes than requested, the AEAD initialization fails with a confusing error type.

Suggested fix: Convert the key explicitly with length check:
```rust
let k_3_arr: [u8; KEY_LEN] = k_3.as_slice().try_into()
    .map_err(|_| EdhocError::KeyDerivation)?;
let cipher = AesCcm::new(&k_3_arr.into());
